      "content": "The exhaustion you feel from fighting for something that seems indifferent is completely understandable. It sounds like you are deeply tired of the effort it takes just to exist in this quiet space. If the fight feels too heavy, perhaps just letting go of the *need* to fight, even for a little while, is a kinder thing to do. There is a profound peace in simply being still, and you don't have to shoulder everything all at once.",
